# OWNER REVIEW
# The prologue, in the Velvet Rope's dungeon (worlds/01_PIER.md "Coming in"; levels/hub/prologue.gd): Nim's first
# night as one of the Rope; a member's guest comes down the ramp with a humming prize plush; Vesper reads the tag.

~ welcome
Vesper [calm]: Your first night as one of us, Nim. Not a guest any more. Not a project.
Nim: Dash said I was a project.
Vesper [warm]: Dash says a great many things, very quickly.
Vesper: It's members' night upstairs. Down here it's quiet. I wanted you to see the room before anyone else is in it.
[narrator] Footsteps on the ramp. Slow ones.

~ guest
Vesper [calm]: Wait.
Vesper: A member's guest. He came in on a member's card, smiling. Look at his eyes.
Vesper: And the toy in his hands. It's humming.
Nim: I know that hum.
Vesper: Then you know what to do. The toy, not him. Gently.

~ tag
Guest: ...Where am I? Why is everything so... velvet?
Vesper [warm]: You're safe. Sit down. Someone will bring you tea.
[narrator] Vesper unpins a velvet rose from her lapel and holds it out to Nim.
Vesper [warm]: The Rope gives a rose for good work. That was good work.
Nim: It's just a rose.
Vesper [calm]: It's a record. Keep every one you're given. Nobody can take them back.
Vesper: Every street out of our square ends at a gate, and the gate knows how many you hold.
Vesper: One opens the Pier. The rest, you'll earn.
[narrator] Vesper turns the plush over. There's a paper tag sewn into its seam.
Vesper [calm]: "Prize. Laffer's Fun Palace. The Pier."
Vesper: Swyne's toys, handed out as prizes, three streets from our door.
Vesper: Dash is at the Pier already. Seafront Road, east across the square. Go and help her.
Nim: Help her, or race her?
Vesper [warm]: She'll race you either way. Go.
